The card stops while the member is away (review H2, and #404's V1 note on the NAS's CPU).
A-NAS pauses the companion when the page has had no input for 60 s, is hidden, or is under
the local console's screen saver; the page owns that state and passes it as the new
`paused` prop. A pause must stop decoding video and every frame loop, but it must not put
the pet to sleep (its loop is a video too) or take the lock (a lock refuses VNAS's commands).

lock-freeze.ts stays the single owner of the animation chain's frozen switch: frozen is now
locked or paused, so a lock that ends during a pause leaves the card frozen, and so does a
pause that ends under a lock. It also says whether a lock holds the card, so that pressing a
card only a pause froze does not release a lock nobody took. runtime.ts holds a flight
during a pause (a lock lets it fly on), keeps where a stopped walk got to, and carries the
flight on at its speed afterwards. When the freeze ends, the frame in front plays on: a
stage's single loop picked again is the same animation and did not switch, so it stayed
still (dsh-pet unfreezes a lock the same way); a pet asleep under the freeze sleeps on
instead of playing an idle animation once. Commands that arrive during a pause are dropped
by the page, not by the card.

